WEBVTT

01:04.167 --> 01:06.778
So they're still waiting at the ER?

01:09.792 --> 01:12.434
No, you don't have to. I'll call again later.

01:12.434 --> 01:14.451
Just let me out here.

01:14.451 --> 01:16.692
You're still pretty far.
Just past the intersection...

01:16.692 --> 01:19.417
In Ah... In Ah!

02:37.126 --> 02:39.062
Excuse me, hold on a second.

02:39.062 --> 02:40.856
Wasn't surgery supposed to start right away?

02:40.856 --> 02:42.065
What's the holdup here?

02:42.065 --> 02:44.985
Hold on a moment, please.

02:46.917 --> 02:48.853
Is our OR still not ready?

02:48.853 --> 02:51.627
Everything's full.
The last one got taken by a VIP case.

02:51.627 --> 02:52.659
What is it?

02:52.659 --> 02:56.034
What about a switch or backup team, then?

02:56.034 --> 02:59.850
You can't just leave him like that.
Do something!

03:00.667 --> 03:02.435
In Ah.

03:03.327 --> 03:05.046
You can pull strings, right?

03:05.046 --> 03:06.798
Make a call to Haemu Hospital, please?

03:06.798 --> 03:10.052
Please, I'm begging you. Help me out?

03:13.930 --> 03:16.224
[Surgery Time]

03:16.224 --> 03:18.077
[Surgery Time, Current Time, Anesthesia Time]

03:31.750 --> 03:36.328
Rest easy. Professor Yoon is
the top trauma surgeon around.

03:36.328 --> 03:38.830
I'll be watching this through till the end.

03:38.830 --> 03:40.123
Thank you, Director.

03:40.123 --> 03:41.891
I'll be off.

03:48.673 --> 03:51.370
[Operating Room]

05:22.834 --> 05:25.167
Are you awake?

05:25.167 --> 05:26.996
Hey.

05:54.090 --> 05:57.729
[Episode 8: Wanting and Resenting]

05:59.804 --> 06:02.292
Catch me if you can.

06:08.209 --> 06:10.690
What is this, a kids' playground?

06:10.690 --> 06:13.151
Hello, patient here.

06:13.151 --> 06:16.513
Just let me rest, please, okay?

06:16.513 --> 06:19.493
Hey, we splurged on this for you,
and you won't even eat?

06:19.493 --> 06:22.834
Forget it. Nothing tastes good right now.
You three finish it.

06:22.834 --> 06:25.831
Oh, poor baby, no appetite?

06:25.831 --> 06:26.993
Tell me if anything sounds good.

06:26.993 --> 06:28.666
I'll make it for you on the spot.

06:28.666 --> 06:30.126
Hey, by the way, lately...

06:30.126 --> 06:32.004
That woman hasn't shown up?

06:32.921 --> 06:34.332
You know, Ms. Joo!

06:34.332 --> 06:35.423
Right?

06:35.423 --> 06:38.000
She was here all the time
when you were knocked out.

06:38.000 --> 06:40.971
Staring at you with this tender look.

06:40.971 --> 06:43.724
But now that you're awake, not once?

06:43.724 --> 06:48.036
Maybe his energy comes back when she shows up?

06:48.036 --> 06:50.851
Your consciousness came back
while she was here, remember?

06:51.898 --> 06:53.756
What's going on between you two?

06:53.756 --> 06:55.936
Doesn't look like just a coworker thing.

06:55.936 --> 06:58.488
Something's up, right?

06:58.488 --> 07:02.633
Are you guys more than just boss and employee?

07:04.376 --> 07:07.998
Drop it already. Seriously, please.

07:07.998 --> 07:10.734
Are you getting shy?

07:10.734 --> 07:14.755
Look at you, so cute.

07:14.755 --> 07:16.424
Quit it. Come on.

08:05.305 --> 08:07.002
Smells amazing.

08:18.251 --> 08:20.778
What is this? Am I your trained puppy?

08:20.778 --> 08:22.780
Toast delivery at the crack of dawn?

08:22.780 --> 08:25.074
Hey, you still came, though.

08:25.074 --> 08:26.657
Fear brought me here, fear.

08:26.657 --> 08:29.048
Who sends twenty-plus texts
for one piece of toast?

08:29.048 --> 08:30.121
Well, then...

08:30.121 --> 08:32.376
What scared you so much
when I was still out cold?

08:32.376 --> 08:34.792
Coming by day and night every single day.

08:34.792 --> 08:37.151
Taking such devoted care of me?

08:39.017 --> 08:41.508
My sisters spilled everything.

08:41.508 --> 08:44.229
Said it was heartbreaking
to watch from the side.

08:46.917 --> 08:48.549
Fear, yeah.

08:50.959 --> 08:52.494
It really got to me.

08:54.709 --> 08:58.000
And as your superior...

08:58.000 --> 09:00.360
Protecting my staff means checking the status.

09:00.360 --> 09:02.587
Dead or alive, you know.

09:14.209 --> 09:18.805
Right, purely staff protection.

09:18.805 --> 09:21.824
While you're at it with the staff protection...

09:21.824 --> 09:24.441
Discharge me too, why don't you?

09:25.385 --> 09:26.818
Me?

09:26.818 --> 09:28.117
Yeah.

09:34.560 --> 09:36.792
Easy, easy with that.

09:36.792 --> 09:38.857
Lots of breakables in there.

09:38.857 --> 09:42.334
Stuck in one hospital room
and somehow your stuff multiplied?

09:42.334 --> 09:45.629
Turns out deliveries reach the room just fine.

09:49.785 --> 09:52.379
What in the world am I even doing right now?

09:53.246 --> 09:56.276
Why's discharging you falling on me?

09:56.276 --> 09:58.251
The stitches in my abs haven't come out yet.

09:58.251 --> 10:01.376
This stuff is heavy,
and nobody else is picking me up.

10:01.376 --> 10:04.732
Isn't this exactly
when staff protection kicks in?

10:06.551 --> 10:07.802
Just you wait.

10:07.802 --> 10:09.126
The second those stitches come out...

10:09.126 --> 10:10.680
your labor is mine.

10:10.680 --> 10:13.167
I'll squeeze every last drop out of you.

10:13.167 --> 10:14.767
Got it.

10:14.767 --> 10:16.645
See, that's what I'm saying.

10:16.645 --> 10:19.564
That whole area is
seriously undervalued right now.

10:19.564 --> 10:21.733
People might say it's old development talk.

10:21.733 --> 10:23.750
But land never lets you down.

10:23.750 --> 10:25.750
Sure thing.

10:25.750 --> 10:28.448
You can't just leave him like that.
Do something!

10:28.448 --> 10:31.120
Please, I'm begging you. Help me out?

10:34.583 --> 10:36.048
Right, brother?

10:37.667 --> 10:39.350
We'll see.

10:40.453 --> 10:43.463
Anyway, this guy always misses the timing.

10:43.463 --> 10:47.342
He isn't keen on tearing that place down.

10:47.342 --> 10:50.556
Lots of folks would lose
their livelihoods, I suppose.

10:50.556 --> 10:52.123
Compensation's on the table.

10:52.123 --> 10:54.052
Nobody's just kicking people out.

10:54.052 --> 10:57.728
Yeah well, my big brother's got a soft heart.

10:57.728 --> 11:00.772
Since we were kids,
he couldn't walk past anyone struggling.

11:00.772 --> 11:04.067
Always giving in, sacrificing.

11:04.067 --> 11:06.453
Our family's been tough for generations...
you know my old man, right?

11:06.453 --> 11:09.296
The fiercest man in all of Korea.

11:10.991 --> 11:13.812
Beats me who my brother takes after.

11:13.812 --> 11:15.704
One thing's certain.

11:15.704 --> 11:17.681
It isn't Dad's side.

11:18.917 --> 11:21.517
Has to be Mom's, definitely Mom's.

11:41.126 --> 11:42.667
Sorry about that.

11:42.667 --> 11:43.667
I'll apologize for him.

11:43.667 --> 11:45.791
He's had way too much to drink.

11:46.709 --> 11:48.917
PR's been contacted. Get the car ready.

11:48.917 --> 11:51.338
I'll bring him down right now.

12:03.959 --> 12:06.055
Ah Jeong, you made it.

12:06.055 --> 12:08.272
Why are you acting out of character?

12:09.803 --> 12:13.141
The board meeting is right around the corner.
How can you be this reckless?

12:14.376 --> 12:16.685
Cut me some slack today.

12:25.167 --> 12:26.724
Joo In Ah.

12:27.364 --> 12:30.753
What exactly is that woman to you?

12:32.614 --> 12:35.549
The woman I'd die alongside.

12:42.595 --> 12:46.021
Seriously, not one emergency umbrella
in this car?

12:46.750 --> 12:50.272
I'll have to stash one in here next time.

12:52.843 --> 12:56.429
If Ah Jeong's home,
why not ask her to bring an umbrella?

12:56.429 --> 12:58.816
No need to go that far...

12:58.816 --> 13:01.992
Looks like a quick shower.
I'll just sit it out.

13:06.583 --> 13:08.917
So why did things end with Ah Jeong?

13:09.651 --> 13:11.123
The reason's a mystery to me, too.

13:11.123 --> 13:13.459
She just up and ghosted me one day.

13:13.459 --> 13:15.072
Didn't you ask her why?

13:15.072 --> 13:17.000
You must have run into her at work.

13:17.000 --> 13:18.592
Never asked.

13:19.452 --> 13:21.756
She kept quiet for a reason.

13:26.334 --> 13:27.607
What?

13:28.253 --> 13:32.037
Would you have pressed her till the end?

13:34.126 --> 13:36.334
If it were me...

13:36.334 --> 13:38.623
If I were in Ah Jeong's shoes...

13:40.116 --> 13:42.263
That's probably what I'd have wanted.

13:45.228 --> 13:48.148
There's this weird thing
where at crucial moments...

13:48.148 --> 13:50.334
I end up hiding what I really feel.

13:51.303 --> 13:53.373
And at the same time...

13:54.000 --> 13:57.156
Part of me wishes
someone would drag me out of it.

13:57.156 --> 14:00.369
Refuse to give up on me no matter what.

14:00.369 --> 14:03.512
A selfish, contradictory feeling
like that creeps in.

14:06.126 --> 14:10.436
Why not just lay it all out honestly then?

14:13.625 --> 14:15.341
Are you serious?

14:15.341 --> 14:18.144
So I should go through with this marriage?

14:18.144 --> 14:19.664
Yeah, dead serious.

14:19.664 --> 14:22.576
What's the alternative, run away together?

14:22.576 --> 14:25.810
Kicked out of home, stripped of everything?

14:25.810 --> 14:27.444
That's not the life I want.

14:27.444 --> 14:30.070
- In Ah.
- And besides...

14:30.070 --> 14:33.459
Naive thoughts about us lasting forever?

14:33.459 --> 14:35.583
Never crossed my mind, not even once.

14:35.583 --> 14:38.699
So drop the guilt
and walk away with a clear head.

14:38.699 --> 14:40.826
Honestly, I'm...

14:40.826 --> 14:42.843
Truly fine.

14:49.418 --> 14:50.999
Probably...

14:50.999 --> 14:54.178
The truth is I don't know how to be happy.

14:58.209 --> 15:01.782
The moment something feels like happiness,
anxiety creeps in.

15:01.782 --> 15:04.667
Am I really someone who deserves this?

15:04.667 --> 15:06.268
Fear takes over.

15:06.268 --> 15:08.385
And I hide, retreat.

15:09.562 --> 15:12.165
Misery feels safe and cozy, after all.

15:19.000 --> 15:20.587
Close your eyes.

15:21.366 --> 15:23.340
Why?

15:23.340 --> 15:26.664
Nothing weird, I promise. Just close them.

15:30.084 --> 15:31.335
There.

15:32.326 --> 15:34.394
What do you hear?

15:35.000 --> 15:36.548
Rain, obviously.

15:36.548 --> 15:39.875
Calm down and really focus on it, alright?

15:53.976 --> 15:57.360
Raindrops hitting the windshield.

15:57.360 --> 15:59.334
And?

15:59.334 --> 16:00.680
And?

16:01.781 --> 16:03.115
The car engine running.

16:03.115 --> 16:04.376
And?

16:07.376 --> 16:09.923
A motorcycle going by outside.

16:10.945 --> 16:12.313
And?

16:17.000 --> 16:18.477
Kids...

16:19.131 --> 16:20.813
laughing in the distance.

16:21.525 --> 16:22.829
And?

16:25.888 --> 16:28.182
Your breathing.

16:28.182 --> 16:29.477
And?

16:34.959 --> 16:36.852
My heart beating.

16:41.917 --> 16:44.381
That's how you feel it.

16:46.575 --> 16:48.258
Happiness,

16:48.258 --> 16:50.621
when you pour your whole heart into it.

16:50.621 --> 16:53.140
And look quietly inside.

16:54.418 --> 16:57.504
It's right there inside you, for sure.

16:57.504 --> 16:59.923
It's always sitting there.

16:59.923 --> 17:01.863
Whenever you want to find it,

17:03.583 --> 17:05.683
find it just like this.

17:37.293 --> 17:39.084
Glad to have you back.

17:39.084 --> 17:40.296
You've been through a lot.

17:40.296 --> 17:42.548
Thank you.

17:42.548 --> 17:44.511
You went through a lot.

17:44.511 --> 17:46.469
But your face is

17:46.469 --> 17:47.888
looking better.

17:47.888 --> 17:50.084
Hospital food must have agreed with you.

17:50.084 --> 17:52.683
Skipping the office does wonders
for the complexion, doesn't it?

17:52.683 --> 17:54.435
Oh, come on now.

17:54.435 --> 17:56.938
His face was always sharp to begin with.

17:56.938 --> 17:59.640
The whole Audit Office lit up with you back.

17:59.640 --> 18:01.459
Glad to have you back.

18:01.459 --> 18:04.946
I really missed you so much.

18:04.946 --> 18:07.032
Tone it down, way too much.

18:07.032 --> 18:09.225
Don't worry about Mr. Ahn one bit.

18:09.225 --> 18:12.116
Legal is hammering away at this right now.

18:12.116 --> 18:13.487
He's going down hard, count on it.

18:13.487 --> 18:15.850
Word is, even his family cut him loose.

18:15.850 --> 18:16.958
Reaping what he sowed, plain and simple.

18:16.958 --> 18:18.375
You've been through a lot.

18:18.375 --> 18:19.389
Yes.

18:19.389 --> 18:21.545
Hey, Team 3 sure adores you.

18:21.545 --> 18:23.923
Boy, were you ever against going at first.

18:23.923 --> 18:25.163
No, you were dying to go.

18:25.163 --> 18:26.905
Yeah, totally itching for it.

18:26.905 --> 18:29.429
Yeah, that's right.

18:29.429 --> 18:31.417
Good day, Ms. Joo.

18:33.474 --> 18:35.468
Good to have you back.

18:35.468 --> 18:36.977
Yes. Good to be back.

18:36.977 --> 18:39.688
Do you have any plans for today?

18:39.688 --> 18:43.041
Almost didn't recognize you.
You're glowing more than usual.

18:46.279 --> 18:49.491
What, was I gloomy before or something?

18:49.491 --> 18:51.742
No, that's not what I meant...

18:51.742 --> 18:53.828
Something good must be in the air, huh?

18:53.828 --> 18:56.206
Like a favorite staff member's comeback maybe?

18:56.206 --> 18:59.038
- Such a warm welcome rolled out for me...
- Mr. Noh.

19:01.167 --> 19:05.093
Looks like a long absence
dulled your office instincts.

19:09.183 --> 19:11.671
Better whip those back into shape fast.

19:18.353 --> 19:20.938
She still can't stand you, it seems.

19:20.938 --> 19:24.651
All that fighting
through the injury for nothing, sad.

19:28.209 --> 19:29.750
Hey, no problem.

19:29.750 --> 19:31.615
This much is nothing.

19:31.615 --> 19:34.792
Noh Ki Jun, Audit Office ace right here.

19:34.792 --> 19:36.500
Thanks.

19:36.500 --> 19:38.889
All right, let's do this.

20:03.440 --> 20:07.234
Every assignment you handed over is done.

20:07.234 --> 20:08.569
[Audit Office, Head Joo In Ah]

20:08.569 --> 20:09.749
[Okey-dokey]

20:11.101 --> 20:13.548
Okey-dokey?

20:17.079 --> 20:19.292
That's harsh.

20:22.751 --> 20:26.230
[That's harsh]
First day back from being sick and...

20:29.334 --> 20:31.968
Hard work earns a meal. I'll treat you.

20:31.968 --> 20:33.013
For real?

20:33.013 --> 20:34.595
When?

20:34.595 --> 20:37.013
[Audit Office, Head Joo In Ah]

20:49.611 --> 20:52.962
Friday evening. Come to my place.

20:58.286 --> 21:00.005
What's wrong?

21:02.418 --> 21:05.267
My back is killing me.

21:27.709 --> 21:29.482
Mr. Noh.

21:29.482 --> 21:31.403
Hey, Doo Gi.

21:31.403 --> 21:35.115
Sorry I never made it to visit
while you were laid up.

21:35.115 --> 21:36.973
No big deal.

21:36.973 --> 21:38.534
If you took a stab wound...

21:38.534 --> 21:41.792
visiting wouldn't be on my list either,
so we're even.

21:41.792 --> 21:44.014
Come on, that's harsh.

21:45.040 --> 21:46.374
By the way...

21:46.374 --> 21:49.145
Got a work thing I wanted to run by you.

21:49.793 --> 21:51.814
Haemu Pharma was your last beat, right?

21:51.814 --> 21:53.013
Yeah, it was.

21:53.013 --> 21:56.500
Anything in particular
you were digging into back then?

21:56.500 --> 21:58.251
What are you talking about?

21:58.251 --> 21:59.389
The handover was complete.

21:59.389 --> 22:01.489
Didn't you check the cloud folder?

22:02.307 --> 22:03.357
Yeah.

22:03.357 --> 22:05.437
Nothing in there caught my eye.

22:05.437 --> 22:06.668
Empty?

22:06.668 --> 22:08.330
Right.

22:10.300 --> 22:12.169
Let me look into it and circle back.

22:12.169 --> 22:14.127
- Got it.
- Right.

22:22.693 --> 22:25.450
A subsidiary audit case was
sitting on my desk, a big one.

22:25.450 --> 22:26.854
Let me see it through to the end.

22:26.854 --> 22:29.062
Get the files squared away
on the department cloud.

22:29.062 --> 22:31.519
Once that's done,
I'll review and handle the handover.

22:35.299 --> 22:38.594
[Handover]

22:38.594 --> 22:40.754
[No search results were found for files
and folders related to Noh Ki Jun Handover]

22:50.126 --> 22:52.566
Jae Hong, you slammed right now?

22:52.566 --> 22:54.583
Listen, I need a favor.

22:54.583 --> 22:58.713
A file I uploaded to the department cloud
just vanished into thin air.

23:07.292 --> 23:10.183
Oh, perfect.

23:20.292 --> 23:22.032
What can I get you?

23:22.032 --> 23:25.391
For someone bouncing back from being sick...

23:25.391 --> 23:27.392
what dish helps with the recovery?

23:27.392 --> 23:28.517
Korean beef is the way.

23:28.517 --> 23:30.756
What's on the menu?

23:30.756 --> 23:33.709
Something easy that looks impressive...

23:33.709 --> 23:37.433
simple but with a sophisticated touch?

23:37.433 --> 23:40.193
Just pack up everything on display here.

23:40.193 --> 23:42.583
- All of it?
- Practice runs are part of the plan.

23:42.583 --> 23:44.342
Got it.

23:53.627 --> 23:56.863
That folder was deleted two days later.

23:56.863 --> 23:59.149
The trace points to Joo In Ah's PC.

24:14.148 --> 24:17.702
[Haemu Pharma]

24:19.611 --> 24:22.330
[Requires Review: Haemu Pharma]

24:33.042 --> 24:35.085
Whole garlic cloves, here we go.

24:35.085 --> 24:37.459
These are getting sliced in half too.

24:37.459 --> 24:40.215
Slicing them too thin kills the flavor.

24:40.215 --> 24:43.510
Keep them chunky and pile on the garlic.

24:43.510 --> 24:47.557
Eating it that way is good
for your health on top of it.

24:57.042 --> 24:58.567
Set the wok on the table.

24:58.567 --> 25:02.750
- A few drops of sesame oil will do.
- Oil first...

25:02.750 --> 25:06.042
- One spoon of garlic going in.
- Oil...

25:06.042 --> 25:08.760
Oil's missing here, oil...

26:04.667 --> 26:07.735
This tastes incredible, oh my.

26:18.891 --> 26:20.270
Hey.

26:21.298 --> 26:23.208
In this early?

26:24.069 --> 26:26.203
Or did you skip going home altogether?

26:32.376 --> 26:35.562
What's going on?

26:39.625 --> 26:41.812
Back on your very first day here,

26:43.950 --> 26:46.843
what was the real reason
you pushed me to Team 3?

26:54.407 --> 26:57.728
Still bitter about the PM assignment?

26:57.728 --> 27:01.315
PM work, by my read, is no small matter.

27:01.315 --> 27:03.326
You've done it firsthand,
so the weight of it must've registered.

27:03.326 --> 27:07.197
How much the private bleeds
into the professional.

27:07.197 --> 27:10.004
Emotions are tangled in,
which makes handling it tricky.

27:10.602 --> 27:12.661
Someone like you,

27:12.661 --> 27:17.270
with that confidence and sharpness of yours,
untouched by what others think,

27:17.270 --> 27:18.723
the call was that you'd pull it off.

27:18.723 --> 27:20.336
Turned out the call was right.

27:25.709 --> 27:27.709
That's the whole of it?

27:27.709 --> 27:29.235
Any other reason?

27:30.917 --> 27:32.594
Nothing else, truly?

27:40.228 --> 27:41.917
[Special Audit Report on Sponsorships
and Governance of J Care Foundation]

27:41.917 --> 27:44.042
J Care Foundation.

27:44.042 --> 27:48.030
Haemu Pharma backs this medical entity
under their CSR initiative.

27:48.030 --> 27:49.613
On its face, nothing wrong there.

27:49.613 --> 27:52.449
Funding hits the place generously, though.

27:52.449 --> 27:55.961
A legal entity with zero name recognition,
zero track record.

28:00.206 --> 28:02.251
So I dug.

28:02.251 --> 28:05.879
Followed the trail, layer after layer,
doggedly all the way down.

28:05.879 --> 28:09.852
[J Care Foundation]

28:09.852 --> 28:12.303
The structure was twisted
into knots, ridiculously so.

28:12.303 --> 28:13.374
[J Care Foundation]

28:14.448 --> 28:17.382
At the end of the line,
the real owner of this entity is...

28:20.811 --> 28:23.218
Vice Chairman Jeon Jae Yeol.

28:23.218 --> 28:25.607
This entity,

28:25.607 --> 28:28.325
Vice Chairman Jeon Jae Yeol founded it,
didn't he?

28:35.179 --> 28:37.120
The floor is yours now.

28:37.120 --> 28:39.081
Is there a connection?

28:39.081 --> 28:42.685
Between this
and the reason I had to be moved to Team 3.

28:45.959 --> 28:47.045
Alright.

28:47.045 --> 28:49.689
Your position needs adjusting.

28:53.677 --> 28:56.932
[Noh Ki Jun Audit Team 1 Handover]

28:56.932 --> 28:58.162
[Permanent Deletion]

29:00.892 --> 29:03.353
[Delete Noh Ki Jun Audit Team 1 Handover
and all subfolders for good?]

29:03.353 --> 29:06.037
[Noh Ki Jun Audit Team 1 Handover file
has been permanently deleted]

29:08.318 --> 29:10.918
Pulling the plug on the investigation,
yes, that was me.

29:13.115 --> 29:15.991
But the Vice Chairman pocketing personal gain,

29:15.991 --> 29:17.929
or anything off
in Haemu Pharma's internal process,

29:17.929 --> 29:19.423
my read was that none of it held up.

29:19.423 --> 29:21.167
But that kind of...

29:21.167 --> 29:24.409
judgment call shouldn't
sit on your shoulders alone.

29:24.409 --> 29:29.084
Reporting up, putting it before the board,
running a special investigation,

29:29.084 --> 29:30.714
isn't that the order of business here?

29:30.714 --> 29:33.260
The substance and the fallout
would've blown out of proportion,

29:33.260 --> 29:36.361
- with everyone turning into political pawns...
- The damage would've landed

29:36.361 --> 29:38.654
on Vice Chairman Jeon Jae Yeol.

29:44.314 --> 29:47.659
Did some kind of favor come your way from him?

29:48.440 --> 29:50.644
He has no clue I even know.

29:59.042 --> 30:00.834
A person as airtight as you

30:00.834 --> 30:02.537
with the line between work
and personal drawn crystal clear,

30:02.537 --> 30:05.321
worried that Jeon Jae Yeol might take a hit,

30:05.321 --> 30:08.684
buried an issue like this by your own hand?

30:11.617 --> 30:14.925
Even if I drop it,
the lid's coming off eventually, so...

30:14.925 --> 30:17.167
one way or the other,

30:17.167 --> 30:19.596
true to who you are,

30:19.596 --> 30:21.854
set the record straight, please.

30:28.651 --> 30:29.692
Mr. Noh.

30:29.692 --> 30:32.267
- In early today.
- Good morning.

30:32.267 --> 30:34.627
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

31:12.148 --> 31:13.860
This feels good.

31:13.860 --> 31:15.421
Refreshing.

31:23.709 --> 31:25.553
You're home?

31:27.583 --> 31:29.226
You're late today.

31:34.520 --> 31:37.752
Hey, have you been drinking?

32:26.084 --> 32:27.809
Yes, Chairperson,

32:27.809 --> 32:29.742
this is Joo In Ah.

32:31.271 --> 32:34.747
There's an additional item to be reported
at tomorrow's board meeting.

32:38.459 --> 32:42.992
The final motion just passed as well.

32:46.792 --> 32:50.012
Head of Audit, would you like to speak?

32:50.766 --> 32:54.501
There's something
the Audit Committee didn't get to earlier

32:54.501 --> 32:56.880
that I'd like to bring before the board now.

32:56.880 --> 32:59.299
Hold on for a second.

32:59.299 --> 33:02.900
Since this wasn't on the agenda in advance,

33:05.126 --> 33:08.519
Director Park Sang Hwan apparently
has something to propose.

33:08.519 --> 33:09.810
The floor is yours.

33:09.810 --> 33:11.520
Yes.

33:11.520 --> 33:15.213
Please bear with me
for raising this so abruptly.

33:16.481 --> 33:18.455
Due to health concerns,

33:18.455 --> 33:19.693
our Chairman

33:19.693 --> 33:23.080
is currently limited
in carrying out official duties.

33:23.080 --> 33:26.658
As a result,
a great deal of key executive decisions

33:26.658 --> 33:31.074
have been falling
on Vice Chairman Jeon Jae Yeol alone.

33:31.074 --> 33:33.748
Yet the Chairman remains in good standing,

33:33.748 --> 33:36.710
and nothing has changed
about him being our symbolic leader

33:36.710 --> 33:41.381
and the spiritual pillar of this group.

33:41.381 --> 33:42.910
With that in mind,

33:42.910 --> 33:45.635
to promote sharper decision-making

33:45.635 --> 33:48.902
and a more stable management environment,

33:50.334 --> 33:52.308
I'd like to put forward MD Jeon Seong Yeol

33:52.308 --> 33:56.636
for appointment as Co-Vice Chairman.

34:05.959 --> 34:08.418
What's wrong with Director Park?

34:08.418 --> 34:10.459
Wasn't he on the Vice Chairman's side?

34:10.459 --> 34:12.720
Looks like he flipped on him.

34:14.084 --> 34:16.182
Quiet down, everyone.

34:17.091 --> 34:20.709
We'll now move to a vote on the motion

34:20.709 --> 34:22.839
that Director Park has put forward.

34:22.839 --> 34:25.532
On the motion to appoint MD Jeon Seong Yeol

34:25.532 --> 34:28.011
as Co-Vice Chairman
alongside Vice Chairman Jeon Jae Yeol,

34:28.011 --> 34:30.071
all directors in favor,

34:30.071 --> 34:32.573
please raise your hands.

35:22.209 --> 35:23.858
Director Park.

35:23.858 --> 35:26.251
I owe this to you. I truly appreciate it.

35:26.251 --> 35:28.462
Time for me to get in line, too.

35:37.789 --> 35:38.876
Congratulations, Vice Chairman.

35:38.876 --> 35:41.251
Right, Ms. Joo.

35:41.251 --> 35:45.630
That last-minute surprise threw me off,
so it slipped my mind,

35:45.630 --> 35:48.096
but you mentioned you had something to report?

35:48.096 --> 35:51.357
Would you be submitting it in writing
or anything like that?

35:51.357 --> 35:53.221
No, there's nothing.

35:53.221 --> 35:56.143
All right then.

36:04.583 --> 36:06.625
Congratulations.

36:06.625 --> 36:08.586
I owe this to you.

36:10.084 --> 36:13.126
I look forward
to your continued guidance and support.

36:13.126 --> 36:15.118
The pleasure is all ours, sir...

36:15.118 --> 36:16.286
[This board meeting was wild]

36:16.286 --> 36:18.079
[Looks like Jeon Jae Yeol's people
all jumped ship to the new Vice Chairman]

36:18.079 --> 36:19.122
No way.

36:19.122 --> 36:21.499
Does this mean we need sign-off
from both Vice Chairmen now?

36:21.499 --> 36:24.127
Geez, who knows where this company is headed.

36:24.127 --> 36:26.798
Doesn't this make things pretty obvious?

36:26.798 --> 36:29.048
The smart move is hopping on the S side.

36:29.048 --> 36:31.509
So I caught wind of this
from the executive secretaries,

36:31.509 --> 36:34.345
Director Park had been
on the Vice Chairman's side from the start,

36:34.345 --> 36:37.017
but he turned on him this time around.

36:37.017 --> 36:39.707
Office politics are no joke.

36:39.707 --> 36:41.418
Hey, look how this turned out.

36:41.418 --> 36:43.146
What did? Who now?

36:43.146 --> 36:45.042
- Me?
- Be honest with me.

36:45.042 --> 36:47.249
I'm on your side.

36:53.334 --> 36:56.300
Yes, that report is...

37:52.924 --> 37:55.723
[Assistant Manager Noh Ki Jun]

38:18.418 --> 38:21.404
The number you've reached is unavailable.
You'll be connected to voicemail

38:21.404 --> 38:22.954
after the tone, and standard rates apply...

38:22.954 --> 38:24.894
[Joo In Ah]

39:02.452 --> 39:05.576
[Joo In Ah]

39:08.291 --> 39:11.115
[Joo In Ah]

40:05.765 --> 40:09.225
[Head of HR Bu Se Yeong]

40:12.897 --> 40:15.043
Do you know what time it is?

40:15.043 --> 40:16.537
Se Yeong.

40:17.500 --> 40:19.878
There's a favor I need from you.

40:23.418 --> 40:25.863
Hey, how can this be sprung on me like this?

40:25.863 --> 40:27.704
Wasn't my U.S. assignment put on hold?

40:27.704 --> 40:30.044
Right, that was just because you were out sick,

40:30.044 --> 40:31.683
so now that you're back
on your feet, off you go.

40:31.683 --> 40:33.364
I'm not fully back to normal yet,

40:33.364 --> 40:34.744
and I've still got
outpatient treatment to deal with.

40:34.744 --> 40:37.004
There are hospitals in the U.S. too,
no need to worry.

40:37.004 --> 40:39.044
The company picks up all the medical bills.

40:39.044 --> 40:41.011
How great is that?

40:41.011 --> 40:42.343
So, has Ms. Joo been told?

40:42.343 --> 40:44.236
About this sudden reassignment?

40:44.917 --> 40:46.516
What are you talking about?

40:46.516 --> 40:48.875
- She's the one who asked for it.
- What?

40:48.875 --> 40:52.000
She wanted your U.S. assignment
fast-tracked as much as possible,

40:52.000 --> 40:53.741
called me at the crack of dawn.

40:53.741 --> 40:55.750
In exchange,
she wanted you promoted right away,

40:55.750 --> 40:59.654
placed at the top branch
and the most comfortable team.

40:59.654 --> 41:01.359
Looks like In Ah...

41:02.376 --> 41:04.570
really does care about you.

41:15.251 --> 41:17.664
[1g Gold Bar Giveaway]

41:25.735 --> 41:29.235
So everything up to this point
was already cleared in the last audit?

41:29.235 --> 41:31.834
Yes, and since there was
a major restructuring this time,

41:31.834 --> 41:33.596
I pulled up a brand-new sheet.

41:33.596 --> 41:36.288
I need a word with you.

41:37.148 --> 41:38.689
Can't you see I'm in the middle of a briefing?

41:38.689 --> 41:41.246
I said let's talk, right this minute!

41:47.408 --> 41:50.429
What's with this behavior?

41:52.457 --> 41:54.843
Hold off until Mr. Ahn is done.

42:05.868 --> 42:07.535
What did you want to say?

42:07.535 --> 42:09.215
Are you really asking like you don't know?

42:09.215 --> 42:11.255
What's going on with the U.S. assignment?

42:12.334 --> 42:14.648
Wasn't it already set for you to go?

42:14.648 --> 42:16.354
It's a great opportunity for you,

42:16.354 --> 42:18.525
and if you're heading there anyway,
sooner is better.

42:18.525 --> 42:20.959
At the California branch,
you'll get exposure to management work

42:20.959 --> 42:22.750
rather than just government relations.

42:22.750 --> 42:25.396
Forget all that. What's the real reason?

42:29.167 --> 42:30.583
Is this somehow...

42:31.834 --> 42:33.971
about J Care Foundation?

42:44.500 --> 42:47.527
I'm not such a clueless pushover
that I can't get the picture.

42:47.527 --> 42:48.875
I was actually beating myself up,

42:48.875 --> 42:51.745
wondering if I pushed you too hard.

42:51.745 --> 42:54.875
I mean, when an old classmate
you've barely heard from suddenly shows up

42:54.875 --> 42:57.439
asking for a single favor,
it's hard to turn down.

42:57.439 --> 43:01.068
You might feel inclined
to cover for an ex's slip-up.

43:01.068 --> 43:04.674
I regretted going overboard
because of my feelings.

43:06.500 --> 43:08.182
No, you weren't overreacting.

43:10.750 --> 43:12.627
I don't think...

43:14.459 --> 43:16.557
I can promise to set things right.

43:25.251 --> 43:26.549
Why not?

43:27.323 --> 43:28.884
Worried Jeon Jae Yeol might take a hit?

43:28.884 --> 43:30.979
Does that weigh on you that much?

43:32.792 --> 43:34.838
Are you going back to him?

43:34.838 --> 43:36.709
Like the Little Prince

43:36.709 --> 43:40.425
heading back to his planet
to see the rose he raised,

43:40.425 --> 43:43.360
is that what you're doing,
going back to Jeon Jae Yeol?

43:45.084 --> 43:47.628
- No, that's not it at all.
- Then...

43:48.532 --> 43:51.453
How on earth am I supposed
to make sense of all of this?

43:51.453 --> 43:52.892
Is it my job...

43:55.875 --> 43:58.263
to make you understand?

44:01.292 --> 44:04.339
You'll be busy prepping for the assignment,
so I'll pull you off duties for now.

44:04.339 --> 44:06.091
Get yourself ready.

44:07.381 --> 44:08.979
[Interview Room]

44:25.983 --> 44:26.998
Hey.

44:26.998 --> 44:28.439
Now that you're shipping off to the U.S.,

44:28.439 --> 44:30.239
you were really laying
into Ms. Joo, weren't you?

44:30.239 --> 44:32.451
Right? My jaw nearly hit the floor.

44:32.451 --> 44:35.731
By the way,
what were you two talking about earlier?

44:39.875 --> 44:42.166
Seriously, it's his own celebration,

44:42.166 --> 44:43.501
so why the long face?

44:43.501 --> 44:45.252
He's been doing nothing but downing shots.

44:45.252 --> 44:47.854
I know, right? On such a happy day.

44:48.542 --> 44:49.778
Oh come on, don't tell me

44:49.778 --> 44:52.179
you're sulking
because you don't want to buy us drinks?

44:52.179 --> 44:53.811
Oh, no way.

44:56.889 --> 44:58.351
Sounds good.

44:58.351 --> 45:01.313
And for next week's Jeju business trip,

45:01.313 --> 45:04.420
Ms. Joo, you should join us as well.

45:04.420 --> 45:05.873
Me?

45:06.639 --> 45:08.554
What's there for the Audit Office to support...

45:08.554 --> 45:10.906
During your assignment,
you worked on the CPK and JV deals.

45:10.906 --> 45:12.947
Bringing along a partner with experience

45:12.947 --> 45:15.459
would make the mood smoother.

45:15.459 --> 45:18.933
Then of course Ms. Joo has to be there.

45:18.933 --> 45:21.542
I'm jealous.

45:21.542 --> 45:24.349
Jeju must be amazing this time of year.

45:44.084 --> 45:46.455
It's my birthday.

45:48.944 --> 45:51.254
How about giving it a try?

45:55.534 --> 45:57.332
What's this?

46:16.719 --> 46:20.436
[Jeon Jae Yeol, Jeju]

46:33.834 --> 46:35.032
Hello.

46:35.032 --> 46:37.255
Let's grab a drink. It's been ages.

46:54.625 --> 46:56.902
You caught what was said
in the meeting earlier, right?

46:56.902 --> 46:58.283
Get next week's trip in order.

46:58.283 --> 47:00.846
Why Joo In Ah, of all people?

47:00.846 --> 47:03.303
There's plenty of reason for her to come along.

47:03.303 --> 47:05.395
She's also acquainted
with the experienced partner.

47:05.395 --> 47:07.572
Aside from that, the real reason.

47:08.882 --> 47:10.648
What are you trying to pull right now?

47:10.648 --> 47:13.225
What are you doing, Vice Chairman?

47:13.225 --> 47:14.625
You're picking fights while drunk,

47:14.625 --> 47:17.558
shipping off some employee overseas
because of personal feelings.

47:17.558 --> 47:20.282
Do you have any idea
what people are saying about you right now?

47:20.282 --> 47:24.097
That MD Jeon will end up as the head,
and you'll be pushed out.

47:24.097 --> 47:25.626
Do you walk away with minimal damage,

47:25.626 --> 47:27.166
or do you get stripped of everything
and tossed aside in disgrace?

47:27.166 --> 47:29.365
That's what everyone's buzzing about.

47:29.365 --> 47:32.055
So at a time like this,

47:32.055 --> 47:36.048
why can't you keep your own feelings in check
and stop slipping up?

47:36.048 --> 47:38.625
I've been used to that kind of talk for ages.

47:38.625 --> 47:40.545
And I have regrets.

47:40.545 --> 47:42.555
About letting it sway me,

47:42.555 --> 47:45.198
about not being honest with my own feelings.

47:47.376 --> 47:48.680
So what then?

47:48.680 --> 47:50.341
What are you planning to do,
following your heart?

47:50.341 --> 47:52.280
Are you going to die alongside Joo In Ah?

47:52.280 --> 47:54.700
After all, isn't she the woman you'd die with?

47:54.700 --> 47:57.801
The one getting emotional right now
seems to be you, not me.

47:57.801 --> 47:59.572
So?

47:59.572 --> 48:02.783
Could you give it all up? For her sake?

48:02.783 --> 48:04.634
If that's what it takes.

48:26.432 --> 48:28.244
What's this?

48:34.192 --> 48:36.794
What made me buy this?
Something I don't even use.

48:37.693 --> 48:41.755
From here on out,
I'm becoming a real minimalist.

48:45.042 --> 48:46.788
Hey, just leave that be.

48:46.788 --> 48:48.572
You think there are no dishes in the U.S.?

48:48.572 --> 48:50.932
Take it for yourself.

48:50.932 --> 48:52.625
Anyway, looking at it now,

48:52.625 --> 48:54.838
it worked out that you moved into this place.

48:54.838 --> 48:58.980
If I had to scramble for a tenant
while I'm off on the U.S. assignment...

49:01.917 --> 49:04.752
Hey, are you even listening?

49:04.752 --> 49:06.376
Ki Jun,

49:06.376 --> 49:09.179
did you know the Vice Chairman and Joo In Ah

49:09.179 --> 49:11.550
are heading to Jeju together next week?

49:13.418 --> 49:15.032
Yeah, I know.

49:15.032 --> 49:17.005
I checked the schedule.

49:17.005 --> 49:21.526
Jeju is where the two of them
took a trip together.

49:21.526 --> 49:24.000
That's how precious the memory is to him,

49:24.000 --> 49:27.133
he's even held
onto the plane tickets all this time.

49:29.373 --> 49:31.472
How modest of him.

49:31.472 --> 49:34.641
So even the rich go to Jeju
for a couple's trip.

49:37.667 --> 49:40.689
Hey, I told you to keep that cup for yourself.

49:41.566 --> 49:43.946
Did you pack everything in?

49:43.946 --> 49:47.153
Hey, set this dish up there too.

49:53.605 --> 49:55.370
You okay?

50:00.917 --> 50:02.252
I'll go get it.

50:02.252 --> 50:04.296
The food we ordered must be here.

50:19.583 --> 50:21.251
What?

50:21.251 --> 50:23.064
Ki Jun.

50:46.255 --> 50:48.167
I'll head out for a bit.

50:48.167 --> 50:50.433
- We're out of bottled water.
- Okay.

50:59.600 --> 51:00.672
What?

51:00.672 --> 51:01.952
Did I commit some kind of crime?

51:01.952 --> 51:02.992
I already explained the whole thing.

51:02.992 --> 51:05.207
I just lent her a room, that's all.

51:06.487 --> 51:08.586
Quit pinching me, will you?

51:11.100 --> 51:12.573
What kind of guy are you?

51:12.573 --> 51:14.337
You've got the woman
who stayed by your sickbed,

51:14.337 --> 51:15.894
and a separate woman
living with you on top of that?

51:15.894 --> 51:17.174
Who do you think you are?
What gives you the right?

51:17.174 --> 51:19.413
I don't have the right.

51:19.413 --> 51:21.181
But here's the thing,

51:22.475 --> 51:24.960
she says she doesn't have feelings for me.

51:24.960 --> 51:26.879
What kind of nonsense are you talking?

51:26.879 --> 51:30.607
How would she act like that
if she didn't have feelings, huh?

51:31.300 --> 51:32.346
I don't know. That's what she's saying.

51:32.346 --> 51:33.893
She says she's into another guy.

51:33.893 --> 51:35.862
So you'd better drop it too.

51:38.560 --> 51:39.626
You complete dimwit.

51:40.396 --> 51:42.876
How can you only go by what she's saying?

51:42.876 --> 51:44.897
Her behavior, expressions,
that look in her eyes,

51:44.897 --> 51:47.112
those are what you should be watching!

51:47.112 --> 51:49.944
Hey, that look in her eyes
while watching you sick? That one?

51:49.944 --> 51:51.740
Oh my gosh!

51:51.740 --> 51:53.617
This is so frustrating.

52:01.559 --> 52:03.392
It's a pleasure, by the way.

52:03.392 --> 52:05.600
Pleasure to meet you, too.

52:05.600 --> 52:08.770
- Nice to see you again.
- Nice to see you again.

52:12.726 --> 52:15.018
I'm glad you like it.

52:15.018 --> 52:17.279
You should try this.

53:45.896 --> 53:49.585
There's this weird thing
where at crucial moments...

53:50.189 --> 53:53.062
I end up hiding what I really feel.

54:16.382 --> 54:18.384
Where's the place in Jeju?

54:18.384 --> 54:19.042
What?

54:19.042 --> 54:21.281
I'm asking where in Jeju Joo In Ah is staying.

54:21.281 --> 54:22.521
Why are you asking,

54:22.521 --> 54:23.962
planning to chase her all the way out there?

54:23.962 --> 54:26.283
I asked you where, right now.

54:28.301 --> 54:30.579
Jeon Jae Yeol, Noh Ki Jun...

54:31.976 --> 54:34.624
both of you have totally lost it.

54:48.080 --> 54:49.793
The terms aren't half bad,

54:49.793 --> 54:51.959
though some fleshing out is needed.

54:51.959 --> 54:55.146
Still, I'd like the investment size
to be a bit larger.

54:55.146 --> 54:57.134
That brings bigger risk along with it.

54:57.134 --> 54:59.094
For CPK, it's all just playing
with money anyway.

54:59.094 --> 55:01.109
There's no soul in it.

55:07.851 --> 55:10.076
Coming back feels good.

55:13.776 --> 55:15.372
Jeju, I mean,

55:16.320 --> 55:20.036
it was our first and last trip together.

55:21.428 --> 55:24.653
We worked hard to line up the vacation
and took the plunge,

55:25.367 --> 55:27.903
yet even back then,
all we did was work like this.

55:31.851 --> 55:33.921
The board composition is what worries me most.

55:33.921 --> 55:35.505
In Ah.

55:40.642 --> 55:43.802
It seems you're having trouble focusing,

55:43.802 --> 55:46.388
so I'll review it on my own
and report back to you separately.

55:46.388 --> 55:48.365
In Ah, hold on a second.

55:49.642 --> 55:51.413
For just a moment, the two of us,

55:52.934 --> 55:55.202
couldn't we be the way we used to?

56:01.934 --> 56:03.820
That's never going to happen,

56:05.053 --> 56:07.309
us going back to the way we used to be.

56:07.309 --> 56:09.523
Then why did you come back to Korea?

56:20.550 --> 56:21.882
Loyalty.

56:23.365 --> 56:25.976
That promise I made to stand by your side,

56:26.679 --> 56:28.472
this is the last bit of loyalty I owe to it.

56:28.472 --> 56:29.810
It's enough for me.

56:29.810 --> 56:32.879
It doesn't matter
if it's loyalty or some other feeling,

56:34.045 --> 56:36.051
just stay right here by my side,

56:36.942 --> 56:38.411
that's all I need.

56:45.309 --> 56:47.387
I won't be doing even that anymore.

56:48.558 --> 56:50.778
Being held captive by that promise,

56:52.875 --> 56:55.109
I made a mistake I shouldn't have made.

56:57.475 --> 56:59.723
And I hurt someone,

57:02.009 --> 57:04.284
someone I should never have hurt.

57:07.934 --> 57:10.447
Are you talking about Mr. Noh?

57:21.892 --> 57:23.794
So that's why I'm telling you,

57:24.710 --> 57:27.387
I'm never coming back to you.

58:53.287 --> 58:56.290
It must be too late, right?

58:56.290 --> 58:58.596
For me to come to you.

59:04.381 --> 59:06.521
Joo In Ah!

59:29.507 --> 59:31.504
Joo In Ah!

59:48.092 --> 59:50.231
Noh Ki Jun...

01:00:05.573 --> 01:00:09.007
Why on earth did you check out so soon,

01:00:09.007 --> 01:00:11.628
after I went all the way out to that hotel...

01:01:55.966 --> 01:01:58.528
[Haemu Audit Team 3]

01:02:01.847 --> 01:02:06.208
[Joo In Ah is in an inappropriate relationship
with a coworker]

01:02:07.853 --> 01:02:10.340
[Joo In Ah is in an inappropriate relationship
with a coworker]

01:02:18.822 --> 01:02:22.770
[Send]

01:02:54.225 --> 01:02:55.946
By the way, something's been bothering me,

01:02:55.946 --> 01:02:59.330
how obvious my feelings for you
might be at work.

01:03:00.072 --> 01:03:01.726
Clear your whole weekend.

01:03:01.726 --> 01:03:03.366
I've booked a pool villa in Sokcho.

01:03:03.366 --> 01:03:05.994
Then you should go
to Mr. Min's club event this weekend.

01:03:05.994 --> 01:03:06.796
What?

01:03:06.796 --> 01:03:08.580
You said you'd be on fire
once we started dating,

01:03:08.580 --> 01:03:10.236
but you're firing work at me
like flames instead.

01:03:10.236 --> 01:03:13.235
Want to stay for some ramyeon?

01:03:13.235 --> 01:03:14.916
Must be fun for you, isn't it,

01:03:14.916 --> 01:03:16.258
stuck between two men?

01:03:16.258 --> 01:03:17.522
I'm getting a divorce.

01:03:17.522 --> 01:03:19.511
I have regrets about everything.

01:03:19.511 --> 01:03:21.440
What are you doing here?
